 ],
 "notes": "I read 35 stations (map nos. 81–114 plus 109B) in the order printed. No keepers are named, which fits the note that reporters are listed under \"Diary from the Stations\". No light characters are given and no station has a type (L.H. or L.V.).\n\nHow the 'other' field is laid out: printed values joined with \"; \" in column order. That order is returns in 6 years, then Value (Roman), then height in Feet. The \"*\" in the \"In 1885\" column is in 'marks'. The column header prints \"Values.\" in the plural.\n\nSub-headings: only two are printed, \"Sutherland\" (81–82) and \"Outer Hebrides\" (83 onward). After that no new heading appears, so I put every row from 83 to 114 under \"Outer Hebrides\" as printed. That is geographically wrong for the Skye, Mull, Argyll, Clyde and Galloway stations (89–114): a sub-heading was probably dropped in the print or the transcription. The section as a whole is WEST COAST OF SCOTLAND.\n\nRows that need care:\n- 84 Stornoway: \"2 lights,\" is in 'other'. Two Values (II. and I.) are grouped by a brace, with one height of 56 on the first line. I treated the brace as part of the values column, not a station mark.\n- 86 Monach Isles: also two lights, braced, with values I. and II. and heights 150 and 62 on separate lines.\n- 93 \"Skerryvore and Hynish / Signal Tower, Tiree,\" runs over two lines (3997–3998), so the fragments give both.\n- 109B Ailsa Craig: no returns count, no value and no height. Its \"1885,\" probably means the station was new or added in 1885. The printed number is \"109B\", with no underscores.\n- Missing columns: 92 Ardnamurchan has no height, and 105 Sanda has no value or height.\n- Trailing commas: kept on names and places as printed. 85 \"Island Ghlais\" has no comma.\n\nSpellings copied as printed:\n- \"Kyleakin, W, Ross,\" has a comma, probably a slip for \"W. Ross\".\n- \"Rhu Stoir\" is Stoer, \"Dhuheartach\" is Dubh Artach, \"Rhuvaal\" is Rubh' a' Mhail, \"Lochindaul\" is Loch Indaal and \"Skervuile\" is Skervuile.\n- 99 Rhuvaal is on Islay, but no place is printed for it.",
